header='''# Episode 08 — Grandma\'s Suitcase Has Everyone\'s Socks! | Home English | Family Story

> **Format:** 80 continuous story shots ×15 seconds = **20:00 story runtime**.
> **Status:** written and illustrated preproduction draft; performed voices, individual motion first frames and finished film remain pending.
> **Story-only:** natural General American family conversation. No drills, quizzes, narrator recaps or viewer countdowns; optional creator practice belongs after the movie.

On a later afternoon, Maya's mother Ruth arrives with six identical packing cubes as family gifts. Dan fills them with the family's clean socks but puts the cubes back in Ruth's suitcase before asking where they belong. A gentle remembered story, a clear admission and six owner-confirmed labels turn a small mistake into an afternoon of cooperation. Ruth's visible cameo is SHOT_001–SHOT_008 only (120 seconds); she rests offscreen afterward.

## Story arc

- **00:00–02:00:** welcome Ruth, receive six gifts, hear a kindly packing memory and respect her quiet break.
- **02:00–05:00:** Dan packs six clean pairs into six gray cubes and mistakenly stores them in the guest suitcase; he admits the assumption.
- **05:00–07:30:** retrieve only family cubes, leave Ruth's closed lavender personal pouch alone and prepare a method.
- **07:30–12:30:** describe, confirm ownership, label and repack one whole pair at a time.
- **12:30–15:30:** verify six pairs/twelve socks, then store six labeled cubes in fixed reachable cubbies.
- **15:30–20:00:** leave the guest room peaceful, wash hands and share an affectionate resolution in the original six seats.

## Performance and state rules

The same six W01 identities continue. Maya and Nina have equal agency; Dan's admission is met with help, never humiliation. Ruth is Maya's mother, not Nina's. Her new lavender-cardigan appearance is a provisional cameo design requiring creator review. No silent new family identity, recording or motion generation is implied. Fifteen seconds is an editorial shot slot; longer loading, walking, storing and handwashing use explicit story-time ellipses. Dialogue stays short enough for action and response. All current socks are clean, dry and paired; no character removes worn clothing. The household washer and dryer remain closed and unused. See [CONTINUITY.md](CONTINUITY.md) for exact owner, container and shelf ledgers.

## Timed story shots

'''
parts=[header]
for i,r in enumerate(rows,1):
 def ts(sec):return f'{sec//3600:02}:{sec//60%60:02}:{sec%60:02}'
 camera=['Warm eye-level medium coverage, maintaining established room axis.','Medium three-quarter coverage with hands and active object visible.','Counter- or child-height medium framing, without adding offscreen characters.','Wide-to-medium composition with clear doorway and storage geography.'][(i-1)%4]
 if r['loc']=='HOME_TABLE':camera='Seated medium coverage from the original dining axis; preserve all six canonical seats.' if i!=80 else 'Wide six-person closing view from the original dining axis, no extra chair or actor.'
 continuity=r['lock'] or 'Preserve W01 identities, Dan\'s LEFT-wrist watch and RIGHT-pocket sides. '+('Ruth appears only in shots001–008; lavender pouch stays closed; keep six family pairs distinct from guest belongings.' if i>8 else 'Ruth is Maya\'s mother; permanent cast designs remain unchanged; six family sock pairs are still at the laundry counter.')
 parts.append(f'''### SHOT_{i:03} | {ts((i-1)*15)}–{ts(i*15)} | {r['title']}

**Visible cast:** {r['cast']}

**Location:** {r['loc']}

**Camera:** {camera}

**Action:** {r['action']}

**Opening state:** {r['opening']}

**End state:** {r['end']}

**Picture:** [BOARD_{(i-1)//4+1:02}.png](assets/storyboards/BOARD_{(i-1)//4+1:02}.png), panel {(i-1)%4+1}. Illustrated draft; creator approval and individual motion first frame pending.

**Continuity:** {continuity}

**Dialogue:**

'''+ '\n\n'.join(f'**{name}:** {line}' for name,line in r['lines'])+'\n\n')
 words=sum(len(line.split()) for _,line in r['lines'])
 assert words<=36,(i,words)
(E/'STORY.md').write_text(''.join(parts))
